    "question": {
      ":question/id": "d80e009a-d9c9-5c4a-85f2-bc9493c1e385",
      ":question/problem": "The vector $a$ is directed horizontally to the right and has magnitude $21$, while the vector $b$ is directed vertically down and has magnitude $28$. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $a + b$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "8a5c3ac9-baba-5ca9-99e9-4ac79d4b60a7",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "de0f16d1-7952-5374-ad30-43194a76f667",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{1}{1225}(a + b)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "becaba16-c83a-5363-8680-845e1f11fbe1",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{1}{28}(a + b)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "54422d8c-33af-5e51-99b7-32b3915186aa",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{1}{49}(a + b)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "8ea1cb87-f50a-57cc-9ebc-fdb4aede4c62",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{1}{35}(a + b)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "485bc6b5-b033-5275-802c-3c1c0bd2967e",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{1}{21}(a + b)"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "8ea1cb87-f50a-57cc-9ebc-fdb4aede4c62"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we have to find $a+b$. The given directions are perpendicular, so the triangle law of addition gives a right triangle.\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $a+b$, we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\n$$\n\nTo find the magnitude, we can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+b|^2&=|a|^2+|b|^2\\\\\n&=21^2+28^2\\\\\n&=441+784\\\\\n&=1225\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{1225}=35\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u&=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{35}(a+b)\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
